# Call-site ledger of uncertainties at sha256:76a5653e686f617a42922d546a239e9efce72e6b35411b7750a1d12dcba03031.
#
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md;
# uncertainties.md shows how this ledger applies them. The operators of
# AffineScalarFunc are not `def`s of their dunder names: ops.py installs
# closures with setattr (ops.add_arithmetic_ops, ops.add_comparative_ops),
# and core.py wraps eight of them again (core.deprecation_wrapper). So an
# operator on a number with uncertainty calls one of these closures, which
# no candidate names: they are written by hand at each site where such an
# operand can arrive (see uncertainties.md, "Operators").
default reject uncertainties.ops.IndexableIter.__getitem__: the subscripted object is not an IndexableIter; the only IndexableIter is the derivatives_args_index of ops._wrap, whose subscripts accept the candidate explicitly
default reject uncertainties.core.Variable.__hash__: no Variable is hashed at this site (no Variable is a key of the dict or set, or an element looked up in it); the sites that hash a Variable accept the candidate explicitly
default reject uncertainties.core.LinearCombination.__bool__: the tested value is not a LinearCombination (it is a float, int, bool, str, list, dict, set, tuple, re.Match, numpy value or a client value); the three tests of AffineScalarFunc._linear_part in umath_core accept the candidate explicitly
default reject uncertainties.ops.add_comparative_ops.__bool__: the tested value is not a number with uncertainty (AffineScalarFunc): the package tests only floats, ints, bools, strs, containers, re.Match objects, numpy values or comparison results there
default reject uncertainties.core.AffineScalarFunc.__repr__: no number with uncertainty is formatted or passed to repr() at this site; the formatted values are strs, floats, ints, classes, the client's tag or the client's format specification
default reject uncertainties.core.Variable.__repr__: no number with uncertainty is formatted or passed to repr() at this site; the formatted values are strs, floats, ints, classes, the client's tag or the client's format specification
default reject uncertainties.core.AffineScalarFunc.__str__: no number with uncertainty is converted to str or formatted with %s at this site; the values are strs, floats, ints, classes, functions, the client's tag or the client's format specification
default reject uncertainties.ops.IndexableIter.__str__: no IndexableIter is converted to str or formatted at this site (the package never formats one; the only IndexableIter is the private derivatives_args_index of ops._wrap)
default reject uncertainties.unumpy.core.matrix.__rmul__: the right operand of this * is not a unumpy.matrix (the operands are floats, ints, tuples, strs, numpy float arrays and matrices, or the client's derivative values, which are client objects); the products of unumpy/core.py that can meet one accept the candidate explicitly

